From: OCCTSwift ecosystem <noreply@secondmouse.au>
Subject: [PATCH] Modeling Data - A trimmed curve or surface refuses a parameter that is not a
 finite number

Geom_TrimmedCurve::SetTrim, Geom2d_TrimmedCurve::SetTrim and the eight argument overload of
Geom_RectangularTrimmedSurface::SetTrim take their two (four) parameters on trust. A nan or an
infinity fails every comparison the constructors make against the range, or loops on it:
 - a basis that is periodic: the surface always hands the parameters to ElCLib::AdjustPeriodic, and
   the curves do when theAdjustPeriodic is set, which shifts a parameter by whole periods until it
   is in range; a nan or an infinity never is. Geom_RectangularTrimmedSurface then recurses
   (UReverse and VReverse call SetTrim again) until the stack ends. Without the adjustment the
   curves are built with the parameter as it is.
 - a basis that is not periodic: every comparison with a nan is false, so neither the order of the
   two parameters nor the range check fires, and an object is built whose bounds are nan; it faults
   or never returns on its first use. An infinity is refused only by a basis whose own bound is
   finite.
The range checks that follow (U1 == U2, parameters out of range) already throw
Standard_ConstructionError, and GeomTools_CurveSet, Curve2dSet and SurfaceSet turn that into a null
record, but they cannot see a nan. Reached from the BREP text and binary readers (a damaged
parameter such as '10 nan nan 0 4' in a Surfaces table), and from any caller of the constructors.

One rule: a parameter that is not finite is refused with Standard_ConstructionError before anything
is compared or adjusted. The check is a throw statement, which the build's No_Exception does not
remove. Precision::Infinite() (2e100), which the unbounded curves and surfaces report for their
bounds, is finite and is accepted as before. A parameter that is only unused (UTrim or VTrim false)
is not looked at.
---
diff --git a/src/ModelingData/TKG2d/Geom2d/Geom2d_TrimmedCurve.cxx b/src/ModelingData/TKG2d/Geom2d/Geom2d_TrimmedCurve.cxx
--- a/src/ModelingData/TKG2d/Geom2d/Geom2d_TrimmedCurve.cxx
+++ b/src/ModelingData/TKG2d/Geom2d/Geom2d_TrimmedCurve.cxx
@@ -31,6 +31,8 @@
 #include <Standard_RangeError.hxx>
 #include <Standard_Type.hxx>
 
+#include <cmath>
+
 IMPLEMENT_STANDARD_RTTIEXT(Geom2d_TrimmedCurve, Geom2d_BoundedCurve)
 
 typedef Geom2d_TrimmedCurve TrimmedCurve;
@@ -101,6 +103,10 @@ void Geom2d_TrimmedCurve::SetTrim(const double U1,
                                   const bool   theAdjustPeriodic)
 {
   bool sameSense = true;
+  if (!std::isfinite(U1) || !std::isfinite(U2))
+  {
+    throw Standard_ConstructionError("Geom2d_TrimmedCurve::parameter is not a finite number");
+  }
   if (U1 == U2)
   {
     throw Standard_ConstructionError("Geom2d_TrimmedCurve::U1 == U2");
diff --git a/src/ModelingData/TKG3d/Geom/Geom_RectangularTrimmedSurface.cxx b/src/ModelingData/TKG3d/Geom/Geom_RectangularTrimmedSurface.cxx
--- a/src/ModelingData/TKG3d/Geom/Geom_RectangularTrimmedSurface.cxx
+++ b/src/ModelingData/TKG3d/Geom/Geom_RectangularTrimmedSurface.cxx
@@ -36,6 +36,8 @@
 #include <Standard_RangeError.hxx>
 #include <Standard_Type.hxx>
 
+#include <cmath>
+
 IMPLEMENT_STANDARD_RTTIEXT(Geom_RectangularTrimmedSurface, Geom_BoundedSurface)
 
 typedef Geom_RectangularTrimmedSurface RectangularTrimmedSurface;
@@ -232,6 +234,12 @@ void Geom_RectangularTrimmedSurface::SetTrim(const double U1,
   }
   else
   {
+    if (!std::isfinite(U1) || !std::isfinite(U2))
+    {
+      throw Standard_ConstructionError(
+        "Geom_RectangularTrimmedSurface::U parameter is not a finite number");
+    }
+
     if (U1 == U2)
     {
       throw Standard_ConstructionError("Geom_RectangularTrimmedSurface::U1==U2");
@@ -283,6 +291,12 @@ void Geom_RectangularTrimmedSurface::SetTrim(const double U1,
   }
   else
   {
+    if (!std::isfinite(V1) || !std::isfinite(V2))
+    {
+      throw Standard_ConstructionError(
+        "Geom_RectangularTrimmedSurface::V parameter is not a finite number");
+    }
+
     if (V1 == V2)
     {
       throw Standard_ConstructionError("Geom_RectangularTrimmedSurface::V1==V2");
diff --git a/src/ModelingData/TKG3d/Geom/Geom_TrimmedCurve.cxx b/src/ModelingData/TKG3d/Geom/Geom_TrimmedCurve.cxx
--- a/src/ModelingData/TKG3d/Geom/Geom_TrimmedCurve.cxx
+++ b/src/ModelingData/TKG3d/Geom/Geom_TrimmedCurve.cxx
@@ -31,6 +31,8 @@
 #include <Standard_RangeError.hxx>
 #include <Standard_Type.hxx>
 
+#include <cmath>
+
 IMPLEMENT_STANDARD_RTTIEXT(Geom_TrimmedCurve, Geom_BoundedCurve)
 
 typedef Geom_TrimmedCurve TrimmedCurve;
@@ -98,6 +100,10 @@ void Geom_TrimmedCurve::SetTrim(const double U1,
                                 const bool   theAdjustPeriodic)
 {
   bool sameSense = true;
+  if (!std::isfinite(U1) || !std::isfinite(U2))
+  {
+    throw Standard_ConstructionError("Geom_TrimmedCurve::parameter is not a finite number");
+  }
   if (U1 == U2)
   {
     throw Standard_ConstructionError("Geom_TrimmedCurve::U1 == U2");
